<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ménfő</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1044</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ménfő was fought on 5 July 1044 near Győr, where Emperor Henry III defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-aba">Samuel Aba</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. Aba was captured and killed soon afterwards, and Henry restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-orseolo">Peter Orseolo</a>, who did homage to him for the kingdom. This subjection to the empire ended when a pagan uprising overthrew Peter in 1046.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-menfo.jpg" alt="Battle of Ménfő" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Márk Kálti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chronicon_Pictum_P050_A_m%C3%A9nf%C5%91i_csata.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
